WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:17.628
<v Host>Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is May twenty-fifth. Today's story: Tokyo might run its trains twenty-four hours a day. Right now, trains stop around midnight. That could change. Let's listen.

00:00:18.228 --> 00:00:25.788
<v News>東京都は、電車を24時間走らせることを考えています。

00:00:26.487 --> 00:00:36.712
<v News>今、東京の電車は夜12時ごろに止まります。朝5時まで電車はありません。

00:00:37.411 --> 00:00:46.076
<v News>夜遅くまで働く人や、外国からの旅行者にとって、これは不便です。

00:00:46.776 --> 00:00:54.048
<v News>まず、金曜日と土曜日の夜だけ、試してみる予定です。

00:00:54.747 --> 00:01:00.531
<v News>使う路線は、山手線と中央線です。

00:01:01.231 --> 00:01:09.823
<v News>でも、夜の間に線路の点検をしているので、安全の問題があります。

00:01:10.524 --> 00:01:21.756
<v News>東京都の担当者は、「安全が一番大切です。よく調べてから決めます」と言いました。

00:01:22.456 --> 00:01:24.087
<v Host>Let's break it down.

00:01:24.688 --> 00:01:26.463
<v Host>The first sentence.

00:01:27.063 --> 00:01:35.176
<v Slow>東京都は、電車を24時間走らせることを考えています。

00:01:35.975 --> 00:01:43.463
<v Host>The Tokyo Metropolitan Government is thinking about running trains twenty-four hours a day. Let's look at the key words.

00:01:44.063 --> 00:01:46.296
<v Vocab>電車

00:01:46.695 --> 00:01:52.959
<v Host>Train. One of the first words you learn in Japanese. You'll use it every day in Tokyo.

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:56.152
<v Vocab>走らせる

00:01:56.552 --> 00:02:06.176
<v Host>To make something run. The base verb means to run. This form means to make something run. Trains run, but people make trains run.

00:02:06.775 --> 00:02:09.656
<v Vocab>考えています

00:02:10.056 --> 00:02:16.848
<v Host>Is thinking about, is considering. It means they are currently thinking about it. No decision yet.

00:02:17.448 --> 00:02:19.032
<v Host>Next sentence.

00:02:19.632 --> 00:02:26.352
<v Slow>今、東京の電車は夜12時ごろに止まります。

00:02:27.151 --> 00:02:30.608
<v Host>Right now, Tokyo's trains stop around midnight.

00:02:31.207 --> 00:02:33.127
<v Vocab>ごろ

00:02:33.527 --> 00:02:40.151
<v Host>Around, approximately. But only for time. For amounts, you use a different word.

00:02:40.752 --> 00:02:43.199
<v Vocab>止まります

00:02:43.599 --> 00:02:48.448
<v Host>Stops. One of the most useful verbs for daily life in Japan.

00:02:49.048 --> 00:02:50.919
<v Host>Who needs this change?

00:02:51.520 --> 00:03:00.807
<v Slow>夜遅くまで働く人や、外国からの旅行者にとって、これは不便です。

00:03:01.608 --> 00:03:07.247
<v Host>For people who work late at night and travelers from abroad, this is inconvenient.

00:03:07.848 --> 00:03:10.295
<v Vocab>働く

00:03:10.695 --> 00:03:15.975
<v Host>To work. A very common verb. You'll hear it in many news stories.

00:03:16.575 --> 00:03:19.048
<v Vocab>旅行者

00:03:19.448 --> 00:03:24.967
<v Host>Traveler. The first part means travel, the last character means person.

00:03:25.568 --> 00:03:27.632
<v Vocab>不便

00:03:28.032 --> 00:03:35.063
<v Host>Inconvenient. The first character is a prefix that means not. The opposite means convenient.

00:03:35.663 --> 00:03:36.840
<v Host>The plan.

00:03:37.439 --> 00:03:45.240
<v Slow>まず、金曜日と土曜日の夜だけ、試してみる予定です。

00:03:46.039 --> 00:03:50.840
<v Host>First, they plan to try it only on Friday and Saturday nights.

00:03:51.439 --> 00:03:53.479
<v Vocab>まず

00:03:53.879 --> 00:03:58.463
<v Host>First, to begin with. A great word for explaining steps.

00:03:59.063 --> 00:04:01.704
<v Vocab>試してみる

00:04:02.104 --> 00:04:08.343
<v Host>To try doing something. When you add this ending to a verb, it means let's try it and see.

00:04:08.943 --> 00:04:11.127
<v Vocab>予定

00:04:11.527 --> 00:04:16.016
<v Host>Plan, schedule. Very useful for everyday conversation.

00:04:16.615 --> 00:04:18.560
<v Host>Which lines will they use?

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:25.375
<v Slow>使う路線は、山手線と中央線です。

00:04:26.175 --> 00:04:35.247
<v Host>The lines they'll use are the Yamanote Line and the Chuo Line. If you've been to Tokyo, you know these. The green circle line and the orange line.

00:04:35.848 --> 00:04:37.983
<v Vocab>路線

00:04:38.384 --> 00:04:42.848
<v Host>Train line, route. Very common in news about transportation.

00:04:43.447 --> 00:04:45.175
<v Host>But there's a problem.

00:04:45.776 --> 00:04:54.992
<v Slow>でも、夜の間に線路の点検をしているので、安全の問題があります。

00:04:55.791 --> 00:05:00.255
<v Host>But they do track inspections during the night, so there are safety concerns.

00:05:00.855 --> 00:05:03.016
<v Vocab>安全

00:05:03.415 --> 00:05:07.735
<v Host>Safety. You'll see this word on signs everywhere in Japan.

00:05:08.336 --> 00:05:10.591
<v Vocab>問題

00:05:10.992 --> 00:05:14.855
<v Host>Problem, issue. Another word you'll hear constantly.

00:05:15.456 --> 00:05:17.543
<v Host>And the official's comment.

00:05:18.144 --> 00:05:26.016
<v Slow>安全が一番大切です。よく調べてから決めます。

00:05:26.815 --> 00:05:32.791
<v Host>Safety is the most important thing. We will investigate carefully before deciding.

00:05:33.391 --> 00:05:35.672
<v Vocab>一番

00:05:36.072 --> 00:05:45.264
<v Host>Number one, the most. You can combine it with any adjective. The most important. The most fun. Very useful pattern.

00:05:45.863 --> 00:05:48.312
<v Vocab>大切

00:05:48.711 --> 00:05:54.759
<v Host>Important, precious. A warm word. You use it for things you truly care about.

00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:57.735
<v Vocab>決めます

00:05:58.136 --> 00:06:02.288
<v Host>To decide. A word you'll use a lot in daily life.

00:06:02.887 --> 00:06:05.887
<v Host>Let's listen to the full story one more time.

00:06:06.487 --> 00:06:14.048
<v News>東京都は、電車を24時間走らせることを考えています。

00:06:14.747 --> 00:06:24.971
<v News>今、東京の電車は夜12時ごろに止まります。朝5時まで電車はありません。

00:06:25.672 --> 00:06:34.336
<v News>夜遅くまで働く人や、外国からの旅行者にとって、これは不便です。

00:06:35.036 --> 00:06:42.307
<v News>まず、金曜日と土曜日の夜だけ、試してみる予定です。

00:06:43.007 --> 00:06:48.791
<v News>使う路線は、山手線と中央線です。

00:06:49.492 --> 00:06:58.084
<v News>でも、夜の間に線路の点検をしているので、安全の問題があります。

00:06:58.783 --> 00:07:10.016
<v News>東京都の担当者は、「安全が一番大切です。よく調べてから決めます」と言いました。

00:07:10.716 --> 00:07:13.451
<v Host>Quiz time. Three questions.

00:07:14.052 --> 00:07:19.980
<v Slow>今、東京の電車は何時に止まりますか？

00:07:20.779 --> 00:07:24.572
<v Host>What time do Tokyo trains stop? Around midnight.

00:07:25.172 --> 00:07:29.803
<v Slow>まず、何曜日に試しますか？

00:07:30.603 --> 00:07:34.588
<v Host>What days will they try first? Friday and Saturday.

00:07:35.187 --> 00:07:39.220
<v Slow>何が一番大切ですか？

00:07:40.019 --> 00:07:43.259
<v Host>What is the most important thing? Safety.

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:45.779
<v Host>Vocabulary recap.

00:07:46.379 --> 00:07:48.612
<v Vocab>電車

00:07:49.012 --> 00:07:50.115
<v Host>Train.

00:07:50.716 --> 00:07:53.163
<v Vocab>止まります

00:07:53.564 --> 00:07:54.788
<v Host>Stops.

00:07:55.387 --> 00:07:57.836
<v Vocab>働く

00:07:58.235 --> 00:07:59.459
<v Host>To work.

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:02.124
<v Vocab>不便

00:08:02.524 --> 00:08:04.012
<v Host>Inconvenient.

00:08:04.612 --> 00:08:06.795
<v Vocab>予定

00:08:07.196 --> 00:08:08.779
<v Host>Plan, schedule.

00:08:09.379 --> 00:08:11.540
<v Vocab>安全

00:08:11.939 --> 00:08:13.187
<v Host>Safety.

00:08:13.788 --> 00:08:16.043
<v Vocab>問題

00:08:16.444 --> 00:08:17.620
<v Host>Problem.

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:20.500
<v Vocab>一番

00:08:20.899 --> 00:08:22.891
<v Host>Number one, the most.

00:08:23.492 --> 00:08:25.939
<v Vocab>大切

00:08:26.339 --> 00:08:27.708
<v Host>Important.

00:08:28.307 --> 00:08:30.684
<v Vocab>決めます

00:08:31.084 --> 00:08:32.427
<v Host>To decide.

00:08:33.028 --> 00:08:45.412
<v Host>That's today's Japanese Daily News. Full transcript with furigana at podcast.jpnotes.dev. Subscribe on Apple Podcasts or Spotify. See you tomorrow.

00:08:46.011 --> 00:08:48.412
<v News>また明日。
